      "writtenOn": "2024-12-09T21:53:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah. So it will context switch to schedule idle for a moment and then because need_resched is preserved, it will trip into schedule again.  It seems unlikely we would be able to do all that while the remote CPU is spinning on the lock, but with crazy numa topologies it seems possible. I\u0027ve not noticed it myself but its something I can try to watch for.",
